    "final_message": "The red acceptance test is written and committed (99a2f6e). It fails at the user story's *then*. tessercheck (zero findings) and `mypy --strict` pass, and the non-root tests pass.\n\n**Test:** `story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`, `TestSubmittingAJtbd::test_a_just_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting`. It submits a JTBD with `POST /jtbds` and gets 201. It then reads `GET /jtbds/{jtbd_id}` until it answers 200, and asserts `check_status.get(\"step\") == \"drafting\"`.\n\n**Failure:**\n```\nE   AssertionError: assert None == 'drafting'\n    where None = ...get('step')\n    where the read answered {'jtbd_id': ..., 'situation': ..., 'motivation': ..., 'outcome': ...}\ntests/test_acceptance.py:46: AssertionError\n```\nThe submit and the read-back both work. The read just has no `step` yet.\n\n**Spec:** `<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v8-sonnet-default/spec.toml`\n- Context `drafting`, aggregate `Jtbd`, identity `jtbd_id`.\n- Fields `situation`, `motivation` and `outcome`, all `str`.\n- Client operations `submit_jtbd` and `check_status`.\n- Orchestrator operation `draft_stories`, action `write_drafts`, repository operations `save_jtbd` and `load_jtbd`, collection `jtbds`.\n- `calling_mode = \"start\"`, because the workflow will later wait on a person.\n- `storage = \"memory\"`, `host = \"http\"`.\n\nThe full run output is in `<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v8-sonnet-default/verify.log`."
